WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.787
Before looking at a sample solution, explain your design.

00:00:03.787 --> 00:00:06.637
The view should have one row per employee.

00:00:06.637 --> 00:00:11.422
It should expose the columns required for employee-department analysis.

00:00:11.422 --> 00:00:16.522
The consuming query should rely on that interface rather than rebuilding the join.

00:00:16.522 --> 00:00:21.822
That is how you demonstrate modular design rather than only SQL syntax.

00:00:21.822 --> 00:00:28.027
Connect this idea to an analytics team exposing a stable reporting view to dashboard users.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:33.552
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:33.552 --> 00:00:41.257
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.257 --> 00:00:46.787
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:46.787 --> 00:00:52.614
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
